\name{cellucid_history_branch_cancel}
\alias{cellucid_history_branch_cancel}
\title{Cancel a new branch}
\usage{
cellucid_history_branch_cancel(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{cancelled} (The name forgotten; null when none was set).
}
\description{
Forget the branch "Branch here" set to start with the next change.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.branch.cancel} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
